rescue — third-party attribution

This file carries a CONDITION. `src/xlix_constants.zig` and
`src/upstream_vectors.zig` reproduce parameter tables and known-answer values
extracted from two third-party projects' source — facebook/winterfell and
miden-crypto — and the MIT terms that material is taken under require each
project's copyright notice and permission text to travel with it. Both texts
are reproduced in full below, and root NOTICE §1 lists this file.

WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, 2026-08-14. Until this revision the tables were recorded
only as provenance — in root NOTICE §2 and in `SPEC.md` — on the reading that
everything this module takes from Winterfell is a black-box test oracle. That
reading does not cover the constants. Winterfell's published permutation KAT is
an oracle; the round-constant tables are not, because they were not observed
from a running program — they were read out of upstream's Rust source by a
script and committed here. Reproduced third-party data owes attribution exactly
as ported source does, the same shape as `bech32` and `brotli`. The RPO half of
this module is unaffected: those constants are derived, not carried (below).

Required attribution — Winterfell Rescue-XLIX parameters
--------------------------------------------------------

Files: `src/xlix_constants.zig`, and the Winterfell-sourced values in
`src/upstream_vectors.zig`.

`ark1` and `ark2` in `src/xlix_constants.zig` — the two 7x12 round-constant
tables of Winterfell's `Rp64_256` — are reproduced from
`crypto/src/hash/rescue/rp64_256/mod.rs` in github.com/facebook/winterfell (the
upstream file's SHA-256 is recorded in the file's own header, alongside the
extraction command and the commit it was taken at). They are embedded rather
than derived because they do not reproduce from the published generator: see
`SPEC.md` §4, "The constants I could not re-derive".

This is DATA extracted from source, not source code: the values are numbers
lifted out of upstream's Rust literals by script and re-emitted as Zig array
literals. No Winterfell Rust source — no function, no control flow, no
comment — is present in this module, and the permutation that consumes these
tables is this repository's own implementation of the published Rescue-Prime
construction.

`src/upstream_vectors.zig` carries two further values taken from the same
project: `winterfell_xlix_perm_in` / `winterfell_xlix_perm_out`, the
`Rp64_256::apply_permutation` known-answer pair from
`crypto/src/hash/rescue/rp64_256/tests.rs`, and `published_inv_alpha`, the
inverse S-box exponent this module also computes for itself. Same character —
numbers extracted by script, no Rust source — and covered by the same notice.

`mds_row` in `src/xlix_constants.zig` is NOT taken from Winterfell in any
load-bearing sense: `params.zig` derives that row independently from the RPO
authors' sage `get_mds`, and `constants_test.zig` asserts the two agree. It is
listed here only because it sits in the same file and shares its header.

